{:edb/db-before-t 2489 :edb/db-after-t 2490 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535802 50 #inst "2026-10-09T07:30:49.016Z" 13194139535802 true] [17592186119802 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367009 13194139535802 true] [17592186119802 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367016 13194139535802 true] [17592186119803 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367023 13194139535802 true] [17592186119804 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367030 13194139535802 true] [17592186119804 1020 #edb/ref 17592186367037 13194139535802 true] [17592186367009 1017 #edb/ref 17592186367010 13194139535802 true] [17592186367009 1089 "q-104151" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367009 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535802 true] [17592186367009 1100 "$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,\\text{_____}⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $r(u,v)$ parametrizes the surface defined in Cartesian coordinates as \n${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{3}=0.$\n What is the third component of $r?$" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367009 1113 #uuid "f8eee31e-0f84-552f-8351-0fc856c749dc" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367009 1145 "First, we write the equation of the surface in the form $z=f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{3} & =0 \\\\ z & =\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, a point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface has the corresponding position vector given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩=⟨x,\\,y,\\,\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, setting $x=u$ and $y=v,$ we obtain the vector function that parametrizes the surface:\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}}⟩\n$$\n\nTherefore, the third component of $r$ is $\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}}.$" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367011 13194139535802 true] [17592186367010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367012 13194139535802 true] [17592186367010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367013 13194139535802 true] [17592186367010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367014 13194139535802 true] [17592186367010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367015 13194139535802 true] [17592186367010 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535802 true] [17592186367010 1041 "selection" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367010 1104 #edb/ref 17592186367013 13194139535802 true] [17592186367010 1110 #uuid "9e84f03c-45f8-5453-9d86-1686a4f61bce" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367011 1034 "\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}}" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367011 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367011 1111 #uuid "72513cd1-ed0c-5758-9f86-3910518bf8b3" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367012 1034 "(u+v)^{3}" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367012 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367012 1111 #uuid "bc35329c-cdb3-52a4-83d0-badeab013971" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367013 1034 "\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}}" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367013 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367013 1111 #uuid "7b8bee01-6009-5cc9-b4da-b11c79f9139e" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367014 1034 "({u}^{2}+{v}^{2})^{3}" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367014 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367014 1111 #uuid "c315d17a-8d08-5f46-a406-dbc6dbf56435" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367015 1034 "(u-v)^{3}" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367015 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367015 1111 #uuid "b041447f-cfcb-557f-8820-7eaa624d4c3e" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367016 1017 #edb/ref 17592186367017 13194139535802 true] [17592186367016 1089 "q-104179" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367016 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535802 true] [17592186367016 1100 "$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,\\text{_____}⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $r(u,v)$ parametrizes the surface defined in Cartesian coordinates as \n$\\frac{x+y}{6}+\\frac{z-1}{2}=\\frac{1}{6}.$\n What is the third component of $r?$" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367016 1113 #uuid "137fac61-848f-5605-9990-3509ba74c2b2" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367016 1145 "First, we write the equation of the surface in the form $z=f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+y}{6}+\\frac{z-1}{2} & =\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ \\frac{z-1}{2} & =\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{x+y}{6} \\\\ \\frac{z-1}{2} & =\\frac{1-x-y}{6} \\\\ z & =\\frac{4-x-y}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, a point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface has the corresponding position vector given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩=⟨x,\\,y,\\,\\frac{4-x-y}{3}⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, setting $x=u$ and $y=v,$ we obtain the vector function that parametrizes the surface:\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,\\frac{4-u-v}{3}⟩\n$$\n\nTherefore, the third component of $r$ is $\\frac{4-u-v}{3}.$" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367018 13194139535802 true] [17592186367017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367019 13194139535802 true] [17592186367017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367020 13194139535802 true] [17592186367017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367021 13194139535802 true] [17592186367017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367022 13194139535802 true] [17592186367017 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535802 true] [17592186367017 1041 "selection" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367017 1104 #edb/ref 17592186367021 13194139535802 true] [17592186367017 1110 #uuid "6285d276-1886-507a-a7a6-cfbc81014574" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367018 1034 "\\frac{4-u-v}{6}" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367018 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367018 1111 #uuid "12c184f9-1c9c-5efb-ae68-bd422886515d" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367019 1034 "\\frac{2-u-v}{6}" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367019 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367019 1111 #uuid "034a13a3-e781-5842-8bf8-06461af74f75" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367020 1034 "\\frac{2-u-v}{3}" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367020 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367020 1111 #uuid "23100d53-d663-5266-82f4-f67d51776d1a" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367021 1034 "\\frac{4-u-v}{3}" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367021 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367021 1111 #uuid "464c331c-2bd2-59f4-b698-2b90c86bc867" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367022 1034 "\\frac{2+u-v}{3}" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367022 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367022 1111 #uuid "893eca1f-0da5-54e8-9c5a-8280aab69731" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367023 1017 #edb/ref 17592186367024 13194139535802 true] [17592186367023 1089 "q-104290" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367023 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535802 true] [17592186367023 1100 "$$\nf(r,\\theta )=⟨r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\text{_____}⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(r,\\theta )$ parametrizes the surface defined in cylindrical polar coordinates as \n$4{r}^{2}-{z}^{2}=0$\nfor $z\\ge 0.$ What is the third component of $f?$" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367023 1113 #uuid "d88762f9-7faa-5003-8c13-d18404076d4e" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367023 1145 "First, we write the equation of the surface in the form $z=f(r,\\theta ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{r}^{2}-{z}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =4{r}^{2} \\\\ z & =\\sqrt{4{r}^{2}} \\\\ z & =2r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the negative solution since we are given that $z\\ge 0.$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical coordinates of a point and $(x,y,z)$ are the corresponding Cartesian coordinates of that point, then we have\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nNow, a point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface has the corresponding position vector given by\n\n$$\nf=⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩=⟨r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $z=2r,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf(r,\\theta )=⟨r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,2r⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the third component of $f$ is $2r.$" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367024 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367025 13194139535802 true] [17592186367024 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367026 13194139535802 true] [17592186367024 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367027 13194139535802 true] [17592186367024 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367028 13194139535802 true] [17592186367024 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367029 13194139535802 true] [17592186367024 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535802 true] [17592186367024 1041 "selection" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367024 1104 #edb/ref 17592186367028 13194139535802 true] [17592186367024 1110 #uuid "b68f42b7-96fb-5fa3-a618-dbefcae9031f" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367025 1034 "{r}^{2}" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367025 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367025 1111 #uuid "ea7900ef-3018-5ff9-878c-a6bd05b1671b" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367026 1034 "r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " 13194139535802 true] [17592186367026 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367026 1111 #uuid "d2141598-0071-5269-b9f5-ad5acf6bad89" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367027 1034 "r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " 13194139535802 true] [17592186367027 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367027 1111 #uuid "f57b53e4-175d-5385-9a33-73a2ae525c48" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367028 1034 "2r" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367028 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367028 1111 #uuid "581f1dde-31e5-5675-ba28-901f6fa21f8e" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367029 1034 "4{r}^{2}" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367029 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367029 1111 #uuid "881e9f53-642e-5201-bfd8-85dc24674352" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367030 1017 #edb/ref 17592186367031 13194139535802 true] [17592186367030 1089 "q-104368" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367030 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535802 true] [17592186367030 1100 "$$\nf(\\theta ,ϕ)=⟨\\text{_____},\\,ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(\\theta ,ϕ)$ parametrizes the surface defined in spherical polar coordinates as \n$\\rho =ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .$\nWhat is the first component of $f?$" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367030 1113 #uuid "eaa8239e-29e5-5977-9d1a-1751cf1acc74" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367030 1145 "If $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\n$$\n\nNow, a point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface has the corresponding position vector given by\n\n$$\nf=⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩=⟨\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $\\rho =ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\theta ,ϕ) & =⟨ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨ϕ{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the first component of $f$ is $ϕ{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ.$" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367031 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367032 13194139535802 true] [17592186367031 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367033 13194139535802 true] [17592186367031 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367034 13194139535802 true] [17592186367031 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367035 13194139535802 true] [17592186367031 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367036 13194139535802 true] [17592186367031 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535802 true] [17592186367031 1041 "selection" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367031 1104 #edb/ref 17592186367033 13194139535802 true] [17592186367031 1110 #uuid "92c2657d-bd5d-577d-93ea-9ecb446ac1e8" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367032 1034 "ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{3}⁡ϕ" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367032 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367032 1111 #uuid "862df4d6-bcbb-53c9-94e3-a7f8b7f06d8b" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367033 1034 "ϕ{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367033 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367033 1111 #uuid "c7567391-d9d3-51c6-9570-dcec53c18ee4" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367034 1034 "ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367034 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367034 1111 #uuid "ce5de037-707f-595f-b502-aaac90e582b1" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367035 1034 "ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡ϕ" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367035 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367035 1111 #uuid "1047f734-e4ef-5ef8-9ff6-2f9e3712abc6" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367036 1034 "ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367036 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [17592186367036 1111 #uuid "144b866d-f52d-5c1c-8a80-0c69d699910c" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367037 1017 #edb/ref 17592186367038 13194139535802 true] [17592186367037 1089 "q-104378" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367037 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535802 true] [17592186367037 1100 "$$\nf(\\theta ,ϕ)=⟨\\text{ _____ },\\,ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(\\theta ,ϕ)$ parametrizes the surface defined in spherical polar coordinates as \n$ϕ=\\rho \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta .$\nWhat is the first component of $f?$" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367037 1113 #uuid "b3e84b4d-aff6-5599-897e-3da92a2fc9f5" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367037 1145 "First, we write the equation of the surface in the form $\\rho =f(\\theta ,ϕ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ϕ & =\\rho \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\rho  & =ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\n$$\n\nNow, a point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface has the corresponding position vector given by\n\n$$\nf=⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩=⟨\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $\\rho =ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta ,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\theta ,ϕ) & =⟨ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the first component of $f$ is $ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ.$" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367038 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367039 13194139535802 true] [17592186367038 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367040 13194139535802 true] [17592186367038 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367041 13194139535802 true] [17592186367038 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367042 13194139535802 true] [17592186367038 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367043 13194139535802 true] [17592186367038 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535802 true] [17592186367038 1041 "selection" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367038 1104 #edb/ref 17592186367040 13194139535802 true] [17592186367038 1110 #uuid "dda4e1ea-8286-5816-9a57-f12f29bb748a" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367039 1034 "ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ" 13194139535802 true] [17592186367039 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535802 true] [1